  "body": "Signed-off-by: Zach Aller <zach_aller@intuit.com>\n",
  "references": [
    {
      "commit": {
        "author": "\"svc-ci\" <code@example.com>",
        "date": "2026-09-18T15:26:12-05:00",
        "subject": "fix(controller): never skip history recalculation when the newest entry has no PR ID (#1955)",
        "body": "shouldSkipHistoryRecalculation (added in #1923) trusted prev.History from\nthe cached CTP read. After the reconcile that writes the promotion-history\nnote and rebuilds history, the PullRequest deletion enqueues another\nreconcile that can read the CTP before that status patch lands. Its stale\nnewest entry (built from the trailer-less squash commit: SHAs matching the\ntip, no PR ID) satisfied every skip condition, so the reconcile re-applied\nthe stale history over the note-derived one and pinned it until the active\ntip moved. This is what made the \"externally squash-merged PR\" spec flake.\n\nTreat a newest entry without a pull request ID as untrusted so the rebuild\npicks the note up on the next pass. Commits with genuinely no PR metadata\nfall back to the pre-#1923 behavior of recalculating each reconcile.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B5aqP1x4gLFd3zuyzKTsWR\n\nSigned-off-by: Zach Aller <allerzach@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "sha": "6af07c2a802a38242ad9307dfa3ace02b749a837",
        "repoUrl": "https://github.com/argoproj-labs/gitops-promoter"
      }
    }
  ]
}
